    mg_ch('1. Document Model & BSON Foundations', 'BSON Data Types & 12-Byte ObjectId Internals', 'bson vs json, mongodb objectid structure, Decimal128, ISODate',
        'MongoDB does not store raw UTF-8 JSON text on disk—it encodes **BSON (Binary JSON)**, adding length prefixes for fast field skipping plus rich types JSON lacks: `ObjectId`, `ISODate` (64-bit UTC ms), `Int32`, `Int64 (Long)`, `Decimal128` (exact financial math!), and `BinData`.',
        ['**12-Byte `ObjectId` Breakdown**: `4 bytes` big-endian Unix timestamp (seconds!) + `5 bytes` process-unique random value + `3 bytes` monotonic counter = 24 hex characters.', '**Built-In Creation Timestamp**: Because the leading 4 bytes are the Unix timestamp, `doc._id.getTimestamp()` extracts creation time without storing a separate `createdAt` field!', '**Financial Precision (`Decimal128`)**: Just like SQL `DECIMAL`, always wrap currency in `NumberDecimal("99.95")` instead of IEEE-754 JS `double` floats!'],
        [['`ObjectId("65f1a...")`', '12 bytes (24 hex chars), roughly time-ordered', 'Sorting by `_id` roughly sorts chronologically (1-second resolution).'], ['`NumberDecimal("19.99")`', '128-bit IEEE 754-2008 decimal floating-point', 'Mandatory for banking, tax, and e-commerce prices!'], ['`ISODate("2026-11-21T...")`', '64-bit integer milliseconds since Unix epoch (UTC)', 'Supports native date math and TTL expiration indexes.']],
        "db.users.find().limit(3)",
