    mg_ch('2. CRUD & Operators Mastery', 'Reading Documents: find(), Projections, Cursors, Sort, Skip & Keyset Pagination', 'mongodb find projection, cursor sort limit skip, mongodb pagination _id',
        '`db.collection.find(filter, projection)` returns a lazy **Cursor** (streaming batches of 101 documents initially), while projections (`{ name: 1, email: 1, _id: 0 }`) reduce network bandwidth and enable **Covered Queries**.',
        ['**Inclusion vs Exclusion Projection Rule**: You **cannot mix** inclusion (`1`) and exclusion (`0`) in the same projection object—the ONLY exception is `{ name: 1, _id: 0 }` (excluding `_id` alongside included fields)!', '**Execution Order of `.sort().skip().limit()`**: Regardless of the order you chain them in JavaScript, `mongod` ALWAYS executes **`sort` -> `skip` -> `limit`**!', '**Avoid Large `.skip(100000)`**: Use range pagination (`{ _id: { $gt: lastSeenId } }`) with `.limit(20)` for constant `O(1)` speed.'],
        [['`find({ active: true }, { name: 1, _id: 0 })`', 'Filters active docs & projects only `name`', 'Mixing `{ name: 1, password: 0 }` throws `Projection cannot have a mix of inclusion and exclusion`!'], ['`.sort({ rating: -1, _id: 1 })`', 'Descending by `rating`, deterministic tie-break by `_id`', 'Always include a unique tie-breaker when paginating sorted lists!'], ['`cursor.batchSize(500)`', 'Controls documents transferred per network `getMore` batch', 'Cursors auto-timeout after 10 minutes of inactivity.']],
        "db.products.find({ category: 'Electronics' }).limit(3)",
        ['**Subtle Pagination Duplicate Bug**: Sorting by a non-unique field like `{ rating: -1 }` with `.skip(10).limit(10)` can return the same product on Page 1 and Page 2! Always append `_id: 1` as the final sort key!'],
        [['question' => 'What is the ONLY exception to MongoDB\'s rule forbidding mixing 1 (inclusion) and 0 (exclusion) in a projection?', 'answer' => 'Excluding _id ({ fieldA: 1, _id: 0 })', 'options' => ['Excluding _id ({ fieldA: 1, _id: 0 })', 'Excluding password', 'Including arrays', 'Using findOne()']], ['question' => 'In what internal order does MongoDB execute cursor.limit(5).skip(20).sort({ age: 1 })?', 'answer' => ' Always sort -> skip -> limit regardless of chaining order', 'options' => [' Always sort -> skip -> limit regardless of chaining order', 'limit -> skip -> sort', 'skip -> limit -> sort', 'Randomly based on RAM']], ['question' => 'Why should you add _id: 1 as a tie-breaker when sorting by non-unique fields during pagination?', 'answer' => 'To guarantee deterministic ordering so documents are not duplicated or skipped across pages', 'options' => ['To guarantee deterministic ordering so documents are not duplicated or skipped across pages', 'MongoDB crashes without _id in sort()', 'It disables WiredTiger cache', 'It compresses BSON']]],
        'Run `db.users.find().limit(2)` and compare network payload size when projecting `{ name: 1, email: 1, _id: 0 }`.'
    ),
    mg_ch('2. CRUD & Operators Mastery', 'Query Selectors: Comparison, Logical, Element ($exists, $type) & Regex', 'mongodb query operators, $gt $in $nin, $exists null trap, mongodb regex index',
        'MongoDB\'s query language expresses rich predicates via `$eq`, `$ne`, `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte`, `$in`, `$nin`, `$and`, `$or`, `$exists`, `$type`, and `$expr`.',
        ['**The `{ field: null }` Trap!**: Querying `{ phone: null }` matches BOTH documents where `phone` is explicitly `null` **AND** documents where the `phone` key does not exist at all! To match strictly explicit `null`, use `{ phone: { $type: "null" } }` (BSON type 10); to match missing keys, use `{ phone: { $exists: false } }`!', '**Index-Friendly Prefix Regex**: `/^Aarav/` (case-sensitive, left-anchored `^`) uses a B-Tree index efficiently, whereas `/Aarav/i` scans every index key!'],
        [['`{ status: { $in: ["paid", "shipped"] } }`', 'Matches any value in array (index-friendly)', 'Prefer `$in` over verbose `$or` on the same field!'], ['`{ phone: null }` vs `{ phone: { $type: 10 } }`', '`null` matches missing OR null; `$type: 10` matches ONLY explicit `null`', 'Classic interview & production bug question!'], ['`{ $expr: { $gt: ["$spent", "$budget"] } }`', 'Compares two fields within the **same** document', 'Standard `{ spent: { $gt: "$budget" } }` compares against the literal string `"$budget"`!']],
        "db.products.find({ price: { \$gt: 100 } })",
        ['Notice that in JavaScript objects, duplicate keys overwrite each other (`{ age: 18, age: 30 }` silently drops `18`!), which is why explicit `$and: [{ $or: [...] }, { $or: [...] }]` is required when combining two `$or` clauses!'],
        [['question' => 'What documents does db.users.find({ middleName: null }) match in MongoDB?', 'answer' => 'Both documents where middleName is explicitly null AND documents where middleName is missing', 'options' => ['Both documents where middleName is explicitly null AND documents where middleName is missing', 'Only documents where middleName is the string "null"', 'Zero documents (syntax error)', 'Only documents with empty strings ""']], ['question' => 'How do you compare two fields within the same document (e.g., discountPrice > retailPrice) in find()?', 'answer' => 'Use $expr: { $gt: ["$discountPrice", "$retailPrice"] }', 'options' => ['Use $expr: { $gt: ["$discountPrice", "$retailPrice"] }', 'Write { discountPrice: { $gt: "$retailPrice" } }', 'Use $lookup on the same document', 'It is impossible in MongoDB']], ['question' => 'Which regex pattern can utilize a standard B-Tree index seek efficiently?', 'answer' => 'Case-sensitive left-anchored prefix regex (/^ORD-2026/)', 'options' => ['Case-sensitive left-anchored prefix regex (/^ORD-2026/)', 'Unanchored substring regex (/2026/)', 'Case-insensitive regex (/ord/i)', 'Lookbehind regex']]],
        'Test querying `products` and filtering high-value items in the playground.'
