    mg_ch('4. Aggregation, Transactions & Distributed Scale', 'ACID Transactions, Replica Sets, Horizontal Sharding & Atlas Vector Search', 'mongodb acid transactions, replica set election oplog, mongodb sharding shard key, atlas vector search',
        'Modern MongoDB delivers full **Multi-Document ACID Transactions** across Replica Sets and Sharded Clusters, automatic high-availability failover via **Raft-like Replica Set Elections**, petabyte horizontal scaling via **Sharding**, and native AI **`$vectorSearch`**.',
        ['**Multi-Document Transactions**: Use `session.withTransaction(async () => { ... })`—it automatically retries `TransientTransactionError` write conflicts! Keep transaction runtime `< 1 second` (default hard limit is `60s`).', '**Replica Set Quorum (Odd Member Count!)**: Deploy **3** (or 5) voting nodes (`Primary + Secondary + Secondary`) so if 1 node goes down, `2/3` forms a strict **majority** and elects a new Primary in ~2–10 seconds! A 2-node replica set **cannot** elect a primary if 1 node fails (`1/2` is not > 50%)!', '**Shard Key Selection**: Never use a monotonically increasing key (`ObjectId` or `createdAt`) with **Ranged Sharding**—all inserts hit a single "hot shard"! Use a high-cardinality compound key (`{ tenantId: 1, createdAt: 1 }`) or Hashed Sharding.'],
        [['`3-Node Replica Set (P-S-S)`', 'Tolerates 1 node failure with automatic election', 'Majority of 3 is 2; never deploy an even number of voting nodes!'], ['`Monotonic Ranged Shard Key`', 'Anti-pattern causing write hotspot on last chunk', 'Use hashed sharding or prefix with high-cardinality `tenantId`!'], ['`$vectorSearch` (Atlas)', 'HNSW approximate nearest-neighbor cosine/dot-product search', 'Powers RAG AI semantic retrieval alongside metadata pre-filters in one DB!']],
        "db.orders.aggregate([\n  { \$group: { _id: '\$status', orderCount: { \$sum: 1 }, revenue: { \$sum: '\$total' } } }\n])",
