    mg_ch('4. Aggregation, Transactions & Distributed Scale', 'Deleting Documents, replaceOne vs updateOne & BulkWrite Operations', 'mongodb deleteOne deleteMany, replaceOne vs updateOne, mongodb bulkWrite',
        'Understand the exact operational differences between `deleteOne()`, `deleteMany({})` (`TRUNCATE` vs `drop()`), `replaceOne()` (whole-document swap keeping `_id`), and mixed **`bulkWrite()`** batches.',
        ['**`deleteMany({})` vs `db.col.drop()`**: `deleteMany({})` removes every document one-by-one while keeping indexes intact (slow on 10M docs!); `db.col.drop()` frees the entire collection + indexes on disk almost instantaneously!', '**`bulkWrite([...])`**: Combines `insertOne`, `updateOne`, `replaceOne`, and `deleteOne` into **1 single network round-trip**!'],
        [['`deleteOne(filter)`', 'Deletes first matching document only', 'Always filter by unique `_id` unless any single match is acceptable.'], ['`replaceOne(filter, newDoc)`', 'Replaces entire document except immutable `_id`', 'Cannot contain `$set` or `$`-prefixed operators!'], ['`bulkWrite(ops, { ordered: false })`', 'Batches mixed writes in 1 round-trip', 'Up to 100,000 operations per batch in modern drivers.']],
        "db.orders.deleteOne({ orderNo: 'ORD-9002' })",
