    mg_ch('4. Aggregation, Transactions & Distributed Scale', 'Change Streams (Real-Time CDC), Connection Pooling & Production Security', 'mongodb change streams watch, mongodb connection pooling maxPoolSize, scram-sha-256 tls',
        'Subscribe to real-time inserts/updates/deletes without polling using **Change Streams (`collection.watch()`)**, reuse TCP/TLS sockets via **Driver Connection Pools**, and lock down clusters with SCRAM-SHA-256 + VPC Peering.',
        ['**Resumable Change Streams (`resumeAfter` token)**: Built on top of the Replica Set `oplog`, every Change Stream event carries a `_id` **Resume Token**—persist the latest token so if your microservice restarts, it resumes from the exact event it left off with zero missed updates!', '**Serverless Connection Pool Storm**: Never call `new MongoClient()` inside every Next.js/Lambda invocation without caching the client on `globalThis`—otherwise 500 concurrent requests open 500×`maxPoolSize` sockets and exhaust Atlas connection limits!'],
        [['`collection.watch(pipeline, { fullDocument: "updateLookup" })`', 'Streams real-time CDC events (requires Replica Set!)', 'Pass `fullDocument: "updateLookup"` to receive the entire updated doc alongside `$set` deltas!'], ['`maxPoolSize=50` (Singleton `MongoClient`)', 'Thread/async-safe shared socket pool', 'Instantiate `MongoClient` **once** at app startup, never per HTTP request!'], ['`SCRAM-SHA-256` / X.509 + TLS 1.3', 'Encrypted auth + wire encryption', 'Scope app users to single DB `readWrite`—never `root`!']],
